    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95">

                <pb facs="0094" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg82"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.24/93: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Asmara</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Asmara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-01-02T12:00:00+03:00">January 2,
                            1943—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 3:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1. Reference my telegram dated December 12, 11 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d95-f1"
                    /> Have just received the following telegram from Ethiopian Foreign Minister</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“I am commanded by His Imperial Majesty<anchor n="2" xml:id="d95-f2"/> to
                        request you to be so good as to convey the expression of his gratefulness to
                        President Roosevelt for the announcement of lease and lend authorization to
                            Ethiopia.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d95-f3"/> Furthermore, I am commanded by
                        His Imperial Majesty to ask you if it is possible for you to call on us to
                        discuss matters of vital importance.[”]</p>
                </quote>
                <p>I recommend appointment Commanding Officer of Eritrea Service Command, Colonel
                    Edwin Clark, graduate of West Point and Harvard Law.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d95-f1" n="1" xml:id="d95-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it suggested “appointment Commanding Officer Eritrea Service Command
                    United States of America as agent lend-lease for Ethiopia” and requested
                    information as to how aid would be extended (884.24/91).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d95-f2" n="2" xml:id="d95-f2-content">
                <p>Haile Selassie I.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d95-f3" n="3" xml:id="d95-f3-content">
                <p>Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, December 12, 1942, p.
                    999.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
